  "notes": [
    "This registry contains shared Environment runtimes already migrated to event-driven wakeup on production main.",
    "Exact-location Grand-Place/Bourse runtimes and NPC/gameplay systems are intentionally excluded.",
    "Autoload alias + path identity is locked so lifecycle coverage cannot remain green after a runtime is silently renamed, duplicated, or rewired.",
    "Registered runtimes may perform local per-frame visibility/LOD work, but must not rediscover production mounts by globally traversing SceneTree from _process/_physics_process.",
    "Every registered node_added watcher must have a guarded disconnect path. Runtimes marked teardown_cleanup_required retain the watcher for runtime-lifetime late-child binding and must disconnect specifically from _exit_tree().",
    "State-retaining shared surface runtimes that track generated or official nodes by instance ID must declare node_removed cleanup centrally, connect it from _ready, disconnect it from _exit_tree and purge retained state from the declared handler.",
    "Scene-bound shared prop runtimes that survive production-scene replacement must also declare node_removed cleanup, release owned roots and stale scene references, and re-arm bounded event-driven discovery without per-frame global scans.",
    "Runtime-lifetime watchers with deferred recovery must also suppress already-scheduled recovery after teardown so a disconnected signal cannot leave a stale deferred SceneTree traversal.",
    "Bounded local subtree waits must abort cleanly when their autoload leaves the SceneTree; a terminal-bind watcher may disconnect normally after success while still guarding in-flight await process_frame work during teardown.",
    "Runtimes marked deferred_bind_teardown_guard_required queue binding work with call_deferred and must set a teardown sentinel in _exit_tree plus guard every declared deferred target against teardown/off-tree execution.",
    "Runtimes that subscribe to signals owned by another runtime must explicitly disconnect those external signals at teardown so callbacks cannot outlive their owner.",
    "Terminal one-shot external runtime subscriptions must also disconnect after successful ready_complete so a ready owner does not retain unnecessary cross-runtime callbacks until teardown, except when the subscription is explicitly retained for production-scene replacement recovery.",
    "Runtimes that attach a generated shared-prop or authored-proxy root directly to Main must remove that owned root synchronously from its parent during autoload teardown so scene content and collision registries cannot outlive their owner.",
    "Runtimes that replace presentation resources owned by another shared runtime must restore only the exact resource they still own at teardown and must never overwrite a later owner."
  ],
